      "id": "cn-warring-states",
      "name": "The Warring States",
      "start": -475,
      "end": -221,
      "region": "divided",
      "icon": "⚔️",
      "description": "After the great state of Jin was partitioned by the Zhao, Wei and Han lineages (453 BCE, recognised by the Zhou king in 403), seven powers — Qin, Chu, Qi, Yan, Zhao, Wei and Han — fought for two and a half centuries with mass infantry armies, iron weapons and walls. Reforming ministers such as Li Kui in Wei, Wu Qi in Chu and Shang Yang in Qin built centralised states; Qin took Sichuan (316), crushed Zhao at Changping (260), ended the Zhou royal house (256) and conquered the other six between 230 and 221 BCE.",
