      "id": "cn-five-dynasties",
      "name": "The Five Dynasties and Ten Kingdoms",
      "start": 907,
      "end": 979,
      "region": "divided",
      "icon": "🗡️",
      "description": "When Zhu Wen deposed the last Tang emperor in 907, five short-lived dynasties — the Later Liang, Later Tang, Later Jin, Later Han and Later Zhou — succeeded one another in the north at Kaifeng and Luoyang, while about ten kingdoms ruled the south and Sichuan: Wu and Southern Tang, Wuyue, Min, Chu, Southern Han, Former and Later Shu, Jingnan and, in Shanxi, the Northern Han. The Later Jin ceded the Sixteen Prefectures around Beijing to the Khitan Liao (938). Zhao Kuangyin of the Later Zhou army founded the Song (960), which absorbed the southern kingdoms by 979.",
