      "name": "The Liao, Western Xia and Jin",
      "start": 907,
      "end": 1234,
      "region": "frontier",
      "icon": "🏹",
      "description": "Abaoji of the Khitans founded the Liao (907/916), which took the Balhae kingdom (926) and the Sixteen Prefectures (938) and made the Song pay silver and silk at Chanyuan (1005). The Tangut Western Xia (1038–1227) ruled the Hexi corridor and the Ordos from Xingqing (Yinchuan). The Jurchen Wanyan Aguda founded the Jin (1115), destroyed the Liao (1125), took Kaifeng and the Song emperors in the Jingkang incident (1127) and ruled north China to the Huai River until the Mongols destroyed the Western Xia (1227) and the Jin (1234).",
